## Summary

Sheep Shearer (Fred the Farmer, north-west of Lumbridge) had no quest script: Fred, The Thing and the hand-in were missing, and varp 179, which the client and Quest Helper read, was never set. This adds it. It replaces the earlier Sheep Shearer and Romeo & Juliet version of this PR: Romeo & Juliet is out and left to #299. Content area from #353.

- Progress is on varp 179 (`varp.sheep`), as in OSRS: 0 not started, 1 started, 1 + the balls of wool handed in, 21 complete. At startup the script checks 21 against the cache dbrow's end state. Rewards: 1 QP, 150 Crafting XP, 60 coins.
- Fred's dialogue follows the wiki transcripts: the three opening options, the offer and start prompt, shears from Fred if the player has none, the spinning help with the spinning wheel map icon box (obj 7670 `crafting_icon_dummy`), the remaining count with the three help options, and the reply about unspun wool.
- Hand-ins: partial deliveries ("You give Fred n balls of wool." / "I need n more before I can pay you."); the last delivery goes straight to "That's the last of them." with no give box. Only unnoted balls of wool count.
- Carrying 20 balls of wool when first asking for the quest: the "In fact Fred, funnily enough..." exchange comes right after "...the small matter of The Thing.", takes 20 balls and completes the quest.
- If the reward can't be given (`setQuestStage` returns false, #339; e.g. coins already at the stack limit), the balls taken are given back with "You don't have enough room for the reward." and the stage stays where it was.
- The Thing (npc 731): Shear and using shears on it give "The... whatever it is... manages to get away from you!"; Talk-to gives "That's a sheep...I think. I can't talk to sheep.". A shearing attempt while holding shears sets a server varbit that unlocks "Fred! Fred! I've seen The Thing!".
- New server-only gamevals, written as `-1` and assigned by `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py`: varp `sheep_shearer_state`; varbits `sheep_shearer_progress` (bits 0-4 of `varp.sheep`) and `sheep_shearer_saw_thing`.
- Review: the interaction tests and their `QuestTalkFixture` are removed, as asked. The stile issue you found is in upstream's shared `StileScript`, so it is fixed separately in its own PR (`fix/stile-approach`); this PR doesn't depend on it.

